description:
Implement an `Observable` class that models a lazy push-based data source.

- `new Observable(subscribeFn)` — `subscribeFn` receives an observer `{ next, error, complete }`
- `subscribe(observer)` — starts the stream; returns `{ unsubscribe() }` to stop it
- `map(fn)` — returns a new Observable that transforms each value with `fn`
- `filter(fn)` — returns a new Observable that only passes values where `fn(value)` is truthy

**Example:**
```js
const nums = new Observable(obs => {
  [1, 2, 3].forEach(n => obs.next(n));
  obs.complete();
});
const results = [];
nums.filter(n => n % 2 !== 0).map(n => n * 10).subscribe({
  next: v => results.push(v),
  complete: () => console.log('done')
});
// results: [10, 30]
```

